# Ingredient Substitutions

Flour and buttermilk ratios from [King Arthur on self-rising flour](https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/blog/2024/01/18/self-rising-flour)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Dairy

### 1 cup Buttermilk

- 1 cup milk
- 1 Tbsp lemon juice or white vinegar

Stir and let it sit 10 minutes until it thickens and curdles.
Plain yogurt or sour cream thinned with milk works too.

### 1 cup Heavy Cream, for cooking

- 3/4 cup whole milk
- 1/4 cup melted butter

This will not whip.
Nothing substitutes for cream in whipped cream.

### 1 cup Sour Cream

- 1 cup plain full-fat Greek yogurt

## Baking

### 1 cup Self-Rising Flour

- 1 cup all-purpose flour
- 1.5 tsp baking powder
- 1/4 tsp salt

### 1 cup Cake Flour

- 1 cup all-purpose flour with 2 Tbsp removed
- 2 Tbsp cornstarch

Sift together twice.

### 1 cup Brown Sugar

- 1 cup granulated sugar
- 1 Tbsp molasses

Use 2 Tbsp molasses for dark brown sugar.

### 1 Egg, in baking

- 1 Tbsp ground flaxseed with 3 Tbsp water, rested 5 minutes
- Or 1/4 cup unsweetened applesauce

Neither works where the egg is doing the structural work, as in a custard or a meringue.

## Pantry

### 1 Tbsp Cornstarch, for thickening

- 2 Tbsp all-purpose flour

### 1 cup Tomato Sauce

- 1/2 cup tomato paste
- 1/2 cup water

### 1 Tbsp Fresh Herbs

- 1 tsp dried herbs

Dried herbs want simmering time, so add them early and add fresh ones at the end.
